{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"===== review.md =====\n## Latent layer\n- R1 İşlek yol, alışılmış iş: developed — “{ar:ٱلسَّبِيلِ, tr:es sebîli, gloss:yol} belirli ve tekildir.” The passage names the water road, well-used road, walkers, old road, repeated habit, and aged camel; it explains how repeated work can form a rival walking track.\n- R2 Yakındaki yoldan uzak düşmek: developed — “{ar:تَّبَيَّنَ, tr:tebeyyene, gloss:açıkça belli oldu} kökü ayrılığı...” It brings together separation, interval, connection, proximity, and distance, then explains how visible evidence can remain near while people’s relation to the path changes.\n- R3 Sessiz meskenin delili: developed — “Âd adının seslendirdiği kökte...” The silent dwelling, sign, blood trace, and sight-reach tract are named and linked to the move from visible remains to an inferred fate and inward discernment; the passage also avoids presenting blood as a historical detail.\n- R4 İki ayrı görünüş: developed — “{ar:تَّبَيَّنَ, tr:tebeyyene, gloss:açıkça belli oldu} ile {ar:وَزَيَّنَ, tr:ve zeyyene, gloss:ve güzel gösterdi} kulağa yaklaşır...” The reading contrasts disclosure with adornment, then develops the adornment, ugly serpent or plant, bad-state, and false-guarantee images through surah context.\n- R5 Çalışan gözün önündeki ağ: developed — “Sözlükte {ar:ٱلسَّبِيلِ, tr:es sebîli, gloss:yol} kökünün nadir bir kullanımı...” The eye veil, mirror-prepared kohl, working and distant-seeing eye, and 29:41 spider house are all present; the reading also says the ayah does not report an actual eye disease.\n- R6 Yağmur sanılan bulut: developed — “Âd’ın başka bir sahnesinde halk...” The rain sense is tied to 46:24’s mistaken reading of the cloud, the water-road image, and the surah’s rain passages; the prose clearly says that ٱلسَّبِيلِ means “road” in this ayah.\n- R7 Basiretten istikamete: developed — “{ar:وَكَانُوا۟ مُسْتَبْصِرِينَ, tr:ve kânû mustebsirîn, gloss:oysa basiret sahibiydiler} geçmişte taşıdıkları...” The section keeps the alternative readings of basiret open and connects insight with guidance, remembrance, repeated practice, and the surah’s closing promise of guidance.\n- removal test: The thesis’s outline would survive ordinary glosses and surah context, but the developed case would not stand unchanged. Removing the rare senses would erase specific arguments about habitual work as a track, silent dwellings as signs, veiled sight, and the rain misreading; the result would be materially thinner.\n\n## Issues\n- [Görüşün ince perdesi] “Sözlükte {ar:ٱلسَّبِيلِ, tr:es sebîli, gloss:yol} kökünün nadir bir kullanımı...” — check: latent — difficulty: “zayıf bir görünüş” becoming “güçlü bir engel” merges two different effects: the eye veil obstructs sight, while 29:41’s spider house exposes the weakness of a supposed refuge. — correction: State the specific link between them, such as the web image or mistaken trust, while keeping their effects distinct.\n- [Süsün verdiği hüküm] “Sözlükler ‘şeytan’ denen çirkin bir yılanı...” — check: latent — difficulty: The rare “spend a night in a bad state” sense is connected to the preceding people found collapsed in their homes, but the reader has to infer how that image sharpens the contrast between beautified work and its bad outcome. — correction: State what the bad-state image adds to that contrast; keep the 29:37 connection bounded as an association.\n- [Süsün verdiği hüküm] “{ar:تَّبَيَّنَ, tr:tebeyyene, gloss:açıkça belli oldu} ile {ar:وَزَيَّنَ, tr:ve zeyyene, gloss:ve güzel gösterdi} kulağa yaklaşır...” — check: evidence — difficulty: The claim that the value shift is not unique to one people is linked to Pharaoh’s placement in 29:39, which describes clear proofs and arrogance rather than beautification. — correction: Let 40:37 establish the repeated beautification-and-diversion pattern; use 29:39 only for Pharaoh’s place in the surrounding sequence.\n\n## Verdict\nAll seven planned